---
/**
 * /adult-drivers-ed/texas/final-exam — "texas adult drivers ed final exam", "adult drivers ed final assessment
 * texas", "how many questions on the texas adult drivers ed test".
 *
 * Rebuilt 2026-10-13 on the hook → answer → loop → funnel recipe (~/Claude/SEO/ADE-PAGE-RECIPE.md). Every number
 * comes from `course` in ade-eligibility.ts (40 questions, 20 signs + 20 laws, 70% on each, three attempts) or
 * ade-texas.json (14 of 20 per bank). What passing does is CLAIM, word for word. §84.40(j): never promise a license.
 */
import AdeGuide from '../../../components/ade/AdeGuide.astro';
import ade from '../../../data/ade-texas.json';
import { course, CLAIM, WAIVER_LAPSE } from '../../../data/ade-eligibility';

const base = '/adult-drivers-ed/texas';

// The one-breath answer: lede and meta description.
const answer = `The Texas adult drivers ed final exam is ${course.finalExamQuestions} questions, ${course.finalExamSigns} on highway signs and ${course.finalExamLaws} on traffic laws. You need ${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part, with ${course.finalExamAttempts} attempts.`;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How many questions are on the Texas adult drivers ed final exam?', a: `${course.finalExamQuestions}, in two parts: ${course.finalExamSigns} questions on highway signs and ${course.finalExamLaws} on traffic laws. You need ${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part. Those are the same two subjects §521.161 requires DPS to test, which is why passing them here ${CLAIM}.` },
  { q: 'What score do I need to pass?', a: `${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part, taken separately, so passing one does not carry the other. Texas sets mastery at 70% for this examination.` },
  { q: 'How many times can I take it?', a: `${course.finalExamAttempts} attempts. If you miss more than 30% of the questions on an attempt, the course retests you using different questions, and you may review the material first. Fail three times and you fail the course.` },
  { q: 'Does it show me the right answers?', a: 'No. Texas requires that the course not identify the correct answer on the final examination, so you get your result without an answer key. Knowledge checks during the course work differently and do show you where you went wrong.' },
  { q: 'Is it open book?', a: 'No one proctors you at home, but the questions are written so the answer is not easily determined without having done the course. Texas requires that, and skimming is the reliable way to fail.' },
  { q: 'What happens after I pass?', a: `Your ADE-1317 certificate is ready the moment you pass, and it shows you passed the highway sign and traffic law portions. That is what DPS relies on. ${WAIVER_LAPSE}` },
];

const next = [
  { href: `${base}/texas-written-knowledge-test`, title: 'What the DPS written test covers', blurb: 'The six things Texas law makes DPS test, and the two this exam satisfies.' },
  { href: `${base}/whats-in-the-course`, title: 'What the six hours cover', blurb: `The ${course.modules} modules the exam questions come from.` },
  { href: `${base}/ade-1317-certificate`, title: 'The certificate you get afterward', blurb: 'Who signs it, how long it takes, and whether it expires.' },
  { href: `${base}/cost`, title: 'What the course costs', blurb: `One price, with all ${course.finalExamAttempts} attempts and the certificate in it.` },
];
---
<AdeGuide
  title={`Texas Adult Drivers Ed Final Exam: ${course.finalExamQuestions} Questions, ${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on Each Part, ${course.finalExamAttempts} Attempts | Road Ready Safety`}
  description={answer}
  url={`${base}/final-exam`}
  eyebrow="The course"
  h1={`The Texas adult drivers ed final exam: ${course.finalExamQuestions} questions, ${course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part, no answer key`}
  lede={`${answer} Pass it and the course ${CLAIM}. A retake is a different exam, you never see an answer key, and one module carries the material for half the questions; all three are below.`}
  faqs={faqs}
  dateModified="2026-10-13"
  updated="October 13, 2026"
  band={{ eyebrow: 'Three attempts included' }}
  next={next}
  sources={[
    { label: '16 TAC §84.503(d)(4), which sets the two test banks, the placement and the retest rule' },
    { label: 'Tex. Transp. Code §521.161 and §521.167', href: 'https://statutes.capitol.texas.gov/Docs/TN/htm/TN.521.htm' },
    { label: 'Texas Program of Organized Instruction, Adult Six-Hour edition, Topic 4.1.9' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">How many questions are on the final exam, and what score passes?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      {course.finalExamQuestions} questions in two parts, and you need {course.finalExamPassPercent}% on each part.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 text-sm font-semibold text-text">Part</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 text-sm font-semibold text-text whitespace-nowrap">Questions</th>
            <th class="py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-text whitespace-nowrap">To pass</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">Part 1 &mdash; Highway signs</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-text leading-6">{course.finalExamSigns}</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">{course.finalExamPassPercent}% ({ade.exam.passPerBank} of {course.finalExamSigns})</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">Part 2 &mdash; Traffic laws</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 text-[15px] font-semibold text-text leading-6">{course.finalExamLaws}</td>
            <td class="py-3 text-[15px] text-text-body leading-6">{course.finalExamPassPercent}% ({ade.exam.passPerBank} of {course.finalExamLaws})</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Texas requires the two parts to be scored separately and drawn from two separate question banks.
      Signs and laws are the two things §521.161 makes DPS test, so the course exam that satisfies those
      portions covers them in equal measure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What happens if I fail, and do I see the right answers?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      You can retake it, up to {course.finalExamAttempts} attempts in all, with different questions on a
      retest, and you never see an answer key.
    </p>
    <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 pl-5 m-0 list-disc marker:text-text-subtle">
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>No answer key.</strong> The rules require the course not to identify the correct answer on the final examination. You are told how you did, not which ones you missed.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>A retake is a different exam.</strong> If you miss more than 30%, the retest draws different questions from the bank, so failing once does not show you the next set.</li>
      <li class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]"><strong>{course.finalExamAttempts} attempts, then the course.</strong> Fail three times and you fail the course rather than trying again indefinitely. You may review the material between attempts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">How do I pass it on the first try?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Give Module 4 your full attention and use the {course.knowledgeChecks} knowledge checks as practice.
      Module 4 is where the signs material lives and where the sign half of the exam comes from. The
      knowledge checks cover the same ground, and they <em>do</em> show you what you got wrong.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      There is no trick. Texas requires the questions to be unanswerable without having done the
      instruction.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] font-bold text-text leading-8" style="font-family:'Outfit',sans-serif;">What does passing do for my DPS test?</h2>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-text-body leading-[30px]">
      Passing it {CLAIM}. Your{' '}
      <a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/ade-1317-certificate`}>{course.certificateCode} certificate</a>{' '}
      is ready the moment you pass and shows those portions as passed. {WAIVER_LAPSE}
      The vision test and the driving skills test stay at DPS; the{' '}
      <a class="underline hover:no-underline" href={`${base}/texas-written-knowledge-test`}>written test page</a>{' '}
      sets out exactly which parts are which.
    </p>
  </section>
</AdeGuide>
